# Verified 2026-08-18: start_server.py is listed below and was still served at
# https://norsk-b2-pro.pages.dev/start_server.py on a freshly created deployment.
# Every file in this directory gets uploaded and published, regardless of what
# is written here. .gitignore does not protect you either — wrangler uploads the
# working directory, not the git tree.
#
# This is how ANTHROPIC_API_KEY leaked: .dev.vars sat here, git-ignored but
# world-readable at /.dev.vars on both the production and staging sites.
#
# The only thing that works is keeping secrets OUT of this directory.
# Local secrets now live in ~/.config/norskb2/.dev.vars — copy it in only for
# the duration of a `wrangler pages dev` session, and delete it before deploying.
#
# A durable fix would be to deploy from a curated subdirectory (e.g. set
# pages_build_output_dir in wrangler.toml to a public/ folder holding only the
# assets meant to be public), so that publishing is opt-in rather than opt-out.
#
